        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "FOR SALE BY PRIVATE TREATY\n23, GLENIDAN COURT, ENFIELD, CO. MEATH. A83 X330.\n\nTo organize a viewing or to place a bid on this property go to www.teamlorraine.ie or scan the QR code on the photograph section of this brochure.\n\nTeam Lorraine Mulligan, national and international award-winning estate agents for over 25 years, is delighted to present No. 23 Glenidan Court (BER B3) an excellent 4/5-bedroom detached family home with a large sunroom to the rear and is located in the highly sought-after and beautifully maintained residential cul-de-sac of Glenidan Court, nestled discreetly in the heart of Enfield. This beautiful home is located on a large corner site and has massive potential.\n\nRoom to Live\nThis spacious and well-maintained home offers a superb layout, including a large sunroom to the rear that opens out to a private, south-facing back garden. This garden is sunny, peaceful, and not overlooked, making it ideal for families or those who enjoy outdoor living. To the rear of the garden is a generous in size and has a detached block-built garage with electricity, suitable for a variety of uses such as a home office, workshop, or studio, subject to the necessary planning permission. \n\nThis pristine home enjoys a very large side garden that brings real options. You could create a home for a family member in the garden or extend the house for a growing family. Builders and investors may see the scope to develop the site further. All of these options are of course subject to the relevant planning permission.\n\nBoth the front and back gardens are beautifully presented with mature lawn areas and apple trees. The front of the property offers ample space for off-street parking (two separate driveways and rear house side parking) in a safe and secure environment and overlooks a small, private, and exceptionally well-maintained green area.\n\nThe accommodation in this home comprises an inviting entrance hallway, a guest W.C., a utility room, a bright and spacious kitchen, a separate dining room ideal for formal meals or family gatherings, a versatile room that can serve as a TV room, playroom, or office, a formal sitting room, and a large sunroom to the rear. Upstairs offers four bedrooms, including a master bedroom with ensuite, and a main family bathroom. The house presents fresh, bright and ready to enjoy. This home is in `turn key` condition.\n\nReady When You Are\nThe house is sold with vacant possession, so there is no chain and no delay on the vendor`s side.\n\nWhat is so special about Glenidan Court?` \nIt is becoming increasingly rare to find newly built homes that offer the same level of interior space combined with such large gardens. Developers today tend to focus on high-density housing with much smaller outdoor areas. For these reasons and more, No. 23 Glenidan Court stands head and shoulders above many other homes currently on the market and truly represents a fine piece of real estate. It is an ideal family home with unlimited potential.\n\nGlenidan Court is a small and exclusive residential estate consisting of 26 properties, with only a select number of detached homes. It recently received awards for its outstanding maintenance, presentation and Community Spirit award a testament to the pride taken by its residents. The location is second to none, with Enfield village and train station within walking distance, offering excellent commuter access to Dublin City Centre. The area is also served by multiple bus routes connecting Enfield to destinations such as Edenderry, Mullingar, Navan, Dublin, and the West of Ireland.\n\nFor sports enthusiasts, Enfield GAA Club, Enfield Celtic FC, and Johnstown House Hotel with its fully equipped gym and swimming pool are all within a ten-minute walk. The M4 motorway is just a short drive away, providing direct access to Kilcock, Maynooth, Celbridge, Leixlip, Dublin, and the west of the country. The community spirit within Glenidan Court is very strong, and the development is extremely well cared for by its residents.\n\nThe village of Enfield itself offers a wide range of local amenities, including the Royal Canal Amenity Park and greenway with scenic walkways and cycle routes heading both east and west. There are also several supermarkets including Tesco, SuperValu, and the recently opened Lidl. Additional amenities include butchers, hair salons, a post office, a credit union, medical and dental centres, restaurants, bars, and more. Primary and secondary schools are within walking distance, and the village also features a local library as well as a Community and Economic Hub.\n\nVIEWINGS ARE SURE TO BE STRONG\n\nTo organize a viewing or to place a bid on this property go to www.teamlorraine.ie or scan the QR code on the photograph section of this brochure.\n\nPLEASE NOTE THAT IT IS OUR COMPANY POLICY THAT ALL VIEWERS MUST HAVE PROOF OF FUNDING.\n"
      },
