        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "DOWNSTAIRS ACCOMMODATION\nHALLWAY: 5.08m x 2.036m\nCoving, radiator cover, under the stair`s storage cupboard with a light, sockets and coat hooks, alarm pad, ceramic tiles, carpet on stairwell.\n\nKITCHEN: 3.74m x 3.28m\nLight fitting, modern fitted kitchen with wall and base units and brushed chrome steel handles `Retro` splash back tiles, work tops, crystal display cabinets, electric Range Master style cooker with ovens, stainless-steel sink with water drinking tap, area fully plumbed, dishwasher, ceramic tiles, breakfast bar area and coffee station, sliding pocket door leading to the utility room. \n\nUTILITY ROOM: 3.25m x 1.61m\nLight fitting, area fully plumbed, fitted pull out drawer unit, stainless steel shelving, American fridge freezer, washing machine, tumble dryer, ceramic tiles, sliding pocket door leading to the kitchen, new composite door leading to the back garden. \n\nDINING ROOM: 4.26m x 3.08m\nDouble doors leading to the sitting room, archway leading to the kitchen, ceramic tiles.\n\nSITTING ROOM: 5.10m x 3.36m2 Coving, feature bay window, blind, marble feature open fireplace and a polished hearth, wooden floor, double doors leading to dining area.\n\nSUNROOM: 6.90m x 4.71m\n2 large roof lights for extra light, recessed lights, blinds, `Palazzetti` style wood chip burning stove which is exceptionally cheap to run, wooden floors, French double doors leading to the patio and stunning south facing back garden.\n\nPLAYROOM/OFFICE: 4.53m x 2.70m\nRecessed lights, wall storage cabinets with shelving, blinds, wooden floor.\n\nGUEST WC: 3.15m x .88m\nRecessed lights, W.C., W.H.B., with a vanity unit, half tiled walls, floor tiles. \n\n\nUPSTAIRS ACCOMMODATION\nLANDING:4.04m x 2.12m\nLight fitting, hot press with an immersion, access to the attic, attic pull down ladder, (attic is insulated and partly floored for convenient storage), carpet.\n\nBEDROOM 1: 3.97m x 2.72m\nLight fitting, blind, Roman blind. fitted wardrobes, carpet.\n\nENSUITE: 3.10m x .88m\nLight fitting, W.C., W.H.B., shower with a Rain power shower head and a handheld shower, half wall tiling, floor tiling.\n\nBEDROOM 2: 3.66m x 3.96m\nLight fitting, blind, curtains, fitted wardrobes, wooden flooring.\n\nBEDROOM 3: 4.25m x 2.97m\nLight fitting, blind, curtains, fitted wardrobes, shelving, wooden flooring.\n\nBEDROOM 4: 2.53m x 2.36m\nLight fitting, blind, curtains, fitted wardrobes, shelving, wooden flooring.\n\nUPGRADED BATHROOM: 2.51m x 1.92m\nRecessed lighting, wall tiling, floor tiling, W.C., W.H.B., with a vanity unit, Led mirror, large walk in wet area shower, with a large rain shower head and a `Mira Elite SE|` electric shower, heated towel rail. \n\n\nFEATURES INTERNAL\nAll light fittings included in sale except hallway, sitting room and dining room\nAll kitchen electrical appliances included in sale as per kitchen and utility section of this brochure\nProperty fully alarmed \nPellet stove (maintenance service August 2026)\nNew hot water insulated cylinder in hot press\nWater softener and drinking filter tap\nAll lights LED\nUnderstairs storage with sockets & light\nAttic ladder & partial floor attic with light\nPower shower in ensuite + ceiling lights\nMain bathroom refurbished (tiling, toilet, waterfall shower, vanity unit, Led mirror)\nNew hot water insulated cylinder in hot press\nAlarm on house & garage\nWired Ring doorbell\nPower shower in ensuite + ceiling lights \nThis property has been loved and looked after\n`Turnkey home` in excellent condition\nNew hot water insulated cylinder in hot press\nLow-maintenance PVC fascia, soffits, and gutters on both house and garage\nNaturally bright and airy home with a lovely ambience\nSunroom to the rear\nSuperbly spacious and a perfect family home\n\nFEATURES EXTERNAL\nCavity Wall insulation\nComposite front & back doors\nTriple glaze French doors to patio\n10 Solar panels & battery\nNew condenser oil burner & HVO Biofuel ready\nDouble glazed windows\nOutside lights\nMature front and back gardens\nVehicular side gate access\nOutside tap\nSunny patio area\nRainwater collection tank behind garage\nGarage with sockets & lights\nOutdoor security sensor lights front and back of property \nProperty located in a quiet cul de sac\nBlock-built garage to the rear with electrics, separate side door, and window\nSafe and secure off street parking two separate drives ways and rear side parking\nFantastic neighbourhood with lovely neighbours and a great sense of community\n\n\nSQUARE FOOTAGE: C. 170.31sqm / 1833sqft\n\nHOW OLD IS THE PROPERTY: This house was built in C. 1996\n\nBACK GARDEN ORIENTATION: South facing private back garden \n\nBER RATING: B3 - 130.96 kWh/m²/yr\n\nBER NUMBER: 119382786\n\nSERVICES: Mains water and mains sewerage.\n\nHEATING SYSTEM: Oil fired central heating and wood pellet stove.\n\nWHEN WAS THE BOILER LAST SERVICED?: 2025\n\nHOW OLD IS THE BOILER?: 2025\n\n\nDISCLAIMER\nNotice to all parties viewing this brochure\n1.This brochure is provided for general guidance only. Nothing in it forms or constitutes an offer, contract, or binding agreement, and none of its contents should be treated as a statement of fact upon which any party can rely.\n2.Neither the Agent nor any member of staff has the authority to make representations or give warranties concerning this property on behalf of the vendor.\n3.Every description, measurement, and reference to condition, permitted use, or occupation has been prepared in good faith and is believed to be accurate at the time of preparation. However, prospective buyers and tenants are advised to verify all such details independently through their own inspection or enquiries rather than relying on this brochure alone.\n4.The Agent provides no warranty or covenant relating to the property. While familiar with its general appearance and layout, the Agent makes no claim to expertise regarding title or planning matters, and responsibility for confirming the sufficiency of such documentation rests entirely with the purchaser.\n5.Confirmation of service availability whether for current or intended use is the responsibility of the purchaser. The Agent offers no guarantees or representations on this matter.\n6.Boundaries, fences, hedges, walls, and ditches are not defined by either the vendor or the Agent, including any determination of party-structure status.\n7.Should any conflict arise between the information in this brochure and the formal contract of sale, the contract of sale will take precedence.\n8.References to \"Vendor\" and \"Purchaser\" throughout this brochure should be read as including \"Lessor\" and \"Lessee,\" or \"Landlord\" and \"Tenant,\" wherever the context applies.\n\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
